comments.body:
**Sub-lemma (S5).** Prove strict decrease is preserved by all term-formation operations, so that **full $\beta$** (firing any redex anywhere) is covered:
- $M\succ M' \Rightarrow MN\succ M'N$;
- $M\succ M' \Rightarrow NM\succ NM'$ (**reduction inside the argument**);
- $M\succ M' \Rightarrow \lambda x.M\succ \lambda x.M'$.

**Why hard.** The case $NM\succ NM'$ requires that plugging a strictly smaller value into the strictly monotone functional $[\![N]\!]$ yields a strictly smaller output — exactly where the *strict* monotonicity of G3 is indispensable. Many simplified proofs only handle head/leftmost reduction and silently omit this case; a complete solution must cover it because $\to_\beta$ is the full congruence closure.
